TITLE:: SDGSampleAnalysis
summary:: the sample editor's numbers, in the language: peak, rms, crest, DC, BS.1770 loudness
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SDGSampleEdit, Classes/SDGSampleEditor, Classes/Signal

DESCRIPTION::
Everything here runs on Signals in sclang: no server, no plugins, and exact
on the samples the file holds. Two passes over the audio are kept, and every
readout after that is arithmetic on them.

code::
(
var sr = 44100, sig = Signal.newClear(sr);
sig.size.do { |i| sig[i] = sin(2pi * 220 * i / sr) * 0.5 };
~st = SDGSampleAnalysis.stats([sig], 0, sig.size);
SDGSampleAnalysis.metrics(~st).postln;                 // peak -6.02 dBFS, rms -9.03 dBFS
SDGSampleAnalysis.metrics(~st, gainDb: -6).postln;     // the same with a gain, on paper
~hops = SDGSampleAnalysis.kHops([sig], sr);
SDGSampleAnalysis.loudness(~hops, sr, 0, sig.size).postln;   // (integrated:, momentaryMax: ...)
)
::


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: stats
Per channel over a range of frames: code::(min:, max:, sum:, sumsq:, clipped:, n:)::.
ARGUMENT:: channels
an Array of Signals.
ARGUMENT:: from
ARGUMENT:: to
the frames, code::[from, to)::; the whole channel when code::to:: is nil.

METHOD:: metrics
What the stats come to with a gain applied and, optionally, the DC of each
channel taken out: code::peak:: (dBFS) and code::peakAmp::, code::rms:: over
every channel, code::crest::, code::dc:: per channel before anything is done,
code::dcAfter::, code::overs:: (would pass full scale), code::clipped::
(samples already at full scale in the source).

METHOD:: kHops
One FloatArray per channel: the mean square of the K-weighted signal in every
20 ms hop, over the first link::#*maxLoudnessSeconds:: at most.

METHOD:: loudness
The loudness of a stretch from the hops: 400 ms blocks every 100 ms, gated at
-70 LUFS and then at 10 LU under the mean, averaged; and the loudest single
block. Channels are summed as the spec does. A stretch shorter than a block is
measured as one block and says code::whole: true::. Answers nil when the
stretch holds no whole hop.
ARGUMENT:: hops
from link::#*kHops::.
ARGUMENT:: sampleRate
ARGUMENT:: fromFrame
ARGUMENT:: toFrame
ARGUMENT:: gainDb
applied before the gates, so the reading is of the sample as it would be saved.

METHOD:: kCoefficients
The two biquads of the K-weighting curve for a sample rate.

METHOD:: gainToCeiling
The gain, dB, that brings a peak amplitude to a ceiling.

METHOD:: dbString
A reading as a window shows it: rounded, code::-inf::, or code::-:: for nil.

METHOD:: hopSeconds
METHOD:: blockSeconds
METHOD:: blockHopSeconds
METHOD:: absoluteGate
METHOD:: relativeGate
METHOD:: maxLoudnessSeconds
The constants of the measurement; BS.1770's by default.
